<BaseLayout
  title="Medical & Regulatory Disclaimer — Progene Bio"
  description="Medical and regulatory disclaimer for Progene Bio IVD rapid tests and POCT devices — intended for professional and distributor use only."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
>

  <h1>Medical &amp; Regulatory Disclaimer</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: 2026-09-12</em></p>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Professional use only</h2>
    <p>
      All in-vitro diagnostic (IVD) test reagents and point-of-care testing (POCT) devices described
      on this website are intended for purchase and use by <strong>professional healthcare
      institutions and qualified distributors</strong>, or for registration and distribution in
      accordance with the medical-device regulations of each importing country. These products are
      <strong>not intended for personal self-diagnosis</strong> of disease.
    </p>

    <h2>Not a diagnostic conclusion</h2>
    <p>
      A reactive (positive) result from any rapid test described here is a <strong>screening
      (presumptive) result</strong>, not a definitive diagnosis. Confirmatory testing by an
      appropriate reference method — performed and interpreted by qualified professionals — is
      required before any clinical or legal decision.
    </p>

    <h2>Regulatory scope</h2>
    <p>
      Regulatory status (CE marking, FDA, NMPA, ISO 13485) varies by product and by market, and is
      stated on a per-product basis. The presence of a marking on one product line does not imply
      the same status across all products. Verify the specific product's regulatory status before
      ordering for a regulated market.
    </p>

    <h2>No medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      The content on this website is provided for business-to-business informational purposes only
      and does not constitute medical advice, a diagnosis, or a treatment recommendation. Consult a
      qualified healthcare professional for any medical question.
    </p>

    <h2>Information accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Product specifications, cut-offs and regulatory information are provided for reference and may
      change. Final specifications are confirmed in the product datasheet, instructions for use
      (IFU) and commercial agreement.
    </p>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
